    <comment>New package: python-mcp-types 2.1.1.

mcp-types carries the wire types for the Model Context Protocol. Upstream splits
it out of the MCP Python SDK monorepo (modelcontextprotocol/python-sdk) at the
same tag as the mcp dist, so 2.1.1 here matches mcp 2.1.1, and mcp 2.x declares
Requires-Dist: mcp-types==2.1.1.

Licence MIT, confirmed from the LICENSE shipped in the tag archive and the PyPI
classifier. Pure Python, noarch, singlespec. Runtime dependencies are pydantic
&gt;= 2.12.0 and typing-extensions &gt;= 4.13.0, both already in Factory; all
BuildRequires resolve there too, so nothing needs to land alongside this.

Built from the upstream tag archive rather than the PyPI sdist because the sdist
carries no tests. The two trees are otherwise identical: diff -r between the
sdist's mcp_types/ and the tag archive's src/mcp-types/mcp_types/ is empty, so
this builds the released code. %check runs the upstream suite, 446 tests per
flavour.

Devel project is science:machinelearning:mcp, alongside python-mcp from the same
upstream monorepo. python-fastmcp is being moved there too (change_devel request
1375071), so the MCP packages live together.

Scope note: this does not imply an imminent python-mcp 2.x bump. mcp 2.x breaks 7
of 9 current Factory consumers and four of them have no upstream release
supporting it, so python-mcp stays on 1.x for now. python-mcp-types is useful and
buildable on its own, and it is one of the two prerequisites for a future
python-fastmcp 4.x, which is NOT submitted.

No file conflict with python-mcp 1.28.1, which ships no mcp_types.</comment>
